# Stage 0 Governance Rule

Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/PROGRAM_CHARTER.md`, `docs/STAGE_0_EXECUTION_PLAN.md`, and `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` before changing anything.

The repository is in Stage 0. Research, governance, licensing analysis, architecture decisions, threat modeling, evaluation design, budgeting, and pilot definition are authorized. Production application implementation is prohibited until `docs/GO_NO_GO_DECISION.md` contains a human-approved `GO`.

Never invent evidence or approvals. Use primary sources, record URLs and retrieval dates, distinguish facts from assumptions, update the canonical status document, work in a dedicated branch, open a focused pull request, and never merge or deploy automatically.

Stop at human decision gates involving customer selection, commercial or network-use licensing obligations, major architecture tradeoffs, critical residual security risk, budget approval, pilot pricing, and the final go/no-go decision.